I would choose Julius Caesar, Napoleon Bonaparte, and Genghis Khan. These three military leaders have had incredible impacts on world history, from the ancient times through to the modern age.

Sure, it seems like an interesting choice. But I would actually bring together some lesser-known but equally fascinating historical figures for a dinner conversation that promises rich and diverse insights:

1. Marie Curie - one of the most brilliant minds in physics, her work on radioactivity has shaped modern medicine and science;
2. Alan Turing - a pivotal figure in computer science whose insights laid the groundwork for today's technological landscape;
3. Wangari Maathai - a pioneer for environmental conservation and women's rights who has inspired countless efforts towards a more sustainable and equitable world;
4. Frederick Douglass - an activist and writer who fought tirelessly against slavery and worked to promote civil rights and equality. 

